on to SLES for SAP Applications 473","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Chapter 18: Introduction to SLES for SAP Applications 473\nTechnical requirements �������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� 475\nSLES for SAP Applications ����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� 475\nLong-term support • 476\nWorkload Memory Protection • 476\nSUSE Linux Enterprise Live Patching • 477\nTrento ����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� 478\nTuning SLES for SAP ������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� 479\nConverting a SLES system to SLES for SAP Applications ������������������������������������������������� 480\nSummary ������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������ 481\nGet This Book’s PDF Version and Exclusive Extras • 481\nTable of Contents xix\nPart V: Practice Exercises 483","tags":[],"links":[],"properties":[],"pageStart":19,"pageEnd":20,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf::23","sourceKey":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","sourceType":"pdf","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide","filePath":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","fileName":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","folder":"2 - Source Material/Books","title":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide","heading":"Chapter 19: Practice Exercises – 1 485","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Chapter 19: Practice Exercises – 1 485\nTechnical requirements �������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� 485\nTips for the exercise �������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� 486\nPractice exercise 1 � ����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� 486\nExercise 1 solution ����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� 489","tags":[],"links":[],"properties":[],"pageStart":20,"pageEnd":20,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf::24","sourceKey":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","sourceType":"pdf","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide","filePath":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","fileName":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","folder":"2 - Source Material/Books","title":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide","heading":"Chapter 20: Practice Exercises – 2 505","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Chapter 20: Practice Exercises – 2 505\nTechnical requirements �������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� 505\nTips for the exercise �������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� 506\nPractice exercise 2 ����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� 506\nExercise 2 solution ���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� 508","tags":[],"links":[],"properties":[],"pageStart":20,"pageEnd":20,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf::25","sourceKey":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","sourceType":"pdf","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide","filePath":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","fileName":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","folder":"2 - Source Material/Books","title":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide","heading":"Chapter 21: Unlock Your Exclusive Benefits 525","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Chapter 21: Unlock Your Exclusive Benefits 525\nOther Books You May Enjoy 531\nIndex 535\nPreface\nLinux is an amazing piece of technology. Inheriting from its UNIX roots and reaching new heights,\nit’s a foundational component of today’s services, computing, and the interconnected world in\nwhich we live. It is everywhere, from smartphones, personal devices, wearables, and routers to\nthe largest supercomputer clusters. From universities to Wall Street and the International Space\nStation, it’s even on Mars. Learning more about it is a basic skill to improve and solidify your\ntechnology background.\nSUSE was founded in 1992 in Germany, becoming early “Linux Experts,” creating the first version\nof Enterprise Linux in 2000, for mainframes: SUSE Linux Enterprise Server. Then it was extended\nto PCs and other architectures. Being true to open source and at the forefront of the technology,\nthe company and the product have evolved, creating its latest release, SUSE Linux Enterprise\nServer 16 (SLES 16), released in November 2025.\nIn this book, we cover the basic skills needed to get started with SLES 16 from a practical per-\nspective, providing examples as well as tips learned from experience “in the trenches.” You will\nbe able to follow it from beginning to end, practicing with each step, while learning about how\nthings are built and why they behave as they do.\nWe really hope you enjoy this book and make the most of it. We expect that, when you finish it,\nyou will end up with strong foundational Linux skills and will love SLES. That’s why we wrote\nthis book: to share our love of Linux and empower you in one of the most amazing technologies\nof our age.\nEnjoy reading! Enjoy practicing!\nPreface xxii\nWho this book is for\nThis book has been written to provide general Linux knowledge to practitioners who would like to\nbecome Sysadmins, DevOps engineers, Site Reliability Engineers (SREs), or platform engineers.\nIt is also useful for developers to better understand the foundational layer of their applications.\nIn general, it is written for anyone who aspires to build and work on IT infrastructures. It will\nalso help anyone seeking to obtain the SUSE Certified Administrator (SCA) certification. Even\nthough it is no substitute for the official training, it is a good reference to obtain a strong base to\nmake the most of the official labs and training. The scope of the book is adjusted to the SCA exam,\nextending it with advice from real-world experience and many practical examples.\nWhat this book covers","tags":[],"links":[],"properties":[],"pageStart":20,"pageEnd":23,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf::26","sourceKey":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","sourceType":"pdf","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide","filePath":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","fileName":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","folder":"2 - Source Material/Books","title":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide","heading":"Chapter 1, Getting SLES 16 Up and Running (Physical and Cloud), covers the installation of SLES,","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Chapter 1, Getting SLES 16 Up and Running (Physical and Cloud), covers the installation of SLES,\nfrom obtaining the software and the subscriptions to the installation of the system itself.","tags":[],"links":[],"properties":[],"pageStart":23,"pageEnd":23,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf::27","sourceKey":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","sourceType":"pdf","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide","filePath":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","fileName":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","folder":"2 - Source Material/Books","title":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide","heading":"Chapter 2, Running Basic Commands and Simple Shell Scripts, explains the daily commands that","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Chapter 2, Running Basic Commands and Simple Shell Scripts, explains the daily commands that\nwill be used during system administration, and how they can be automated using shell scripting.","tags":[],"links":[],"properties":[],"pageStart":23,"pageEnd":23,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf::28","sourceKey":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","sourceType":"pdf","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide","filePath":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","fileName":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","folder":"2 - Source Material/Books","title":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide","heading":"Chapter 3, Managing Regular Operations with Tools, shows which simple tools are available in our","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Chapter 3, Managing Regular Operations with Tools, shows which simple tools are available in our\nsystem that can be used for regular daily operations, such as starting or enabling a system service\nor reviewing what is going on in the system by checking logs.","tags":[],"links":[],"properties":[],"pageStart":23,"pageEnd":23,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf::29","sourceKey":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","sourceType":"pdf","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide","filePath":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","fileName":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","folder":"2 - Source Material/Books","title":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide","heading":"Chapter 4, Securing the System with Users, Groups, and Permissions, covers how to manage users,","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Chapter 4, Securing the System with Users, Groups, and Permissions, covers how to manage users,\ngroups, and permissions in a Linux system.","tags":[],"links":[],"properties":[],"pageStart":23,"pageEnd":23,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf::30","sourceKey":"2 - Source Material/Books/suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguide.pdf","sourceType":"pdf","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"suselinuxenterpriseserver16officialadministrationguid